  "about": "The basemap extract for examples/descent: world → Sweden → central Stockholm, only the tiles along that camera path at the zooms it reaches (docs/09-geo.md, camera-aware extraction). Rebuild: cargo run --release -p datars-geo-build -- tiles assets/tiles/descent.job.json --data <inputs dir> --out assets/tiles/descent.pmtiles. Inputs: Natural Earth (public domain) and OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL) — Natural Earth GeoJSON, osmdata land polygons and Overpass extracts converted with datars-geo-build osm, in one inputs directory. Every layer of a zoom band covers at most the band's land region: a tile that exists without its land would draw as sea.",
